	<brief_description>
		What everyone is allowed to know about the match.
	</brief_description>
	<description>
		Created by the [World] rather than by the game mode, because the game mode is the server's alone while this has to exist on clients too - that split is the whole reason the class is separate. It holds the [PlayerState] of every player, on every peer.
		[method get_server_world_time_seconds] gives the server's clock as this peer best knows it, so a timer started on the server reads the same everywhere. Extend it in GDScript for anything the whole match shares - the score, the round number, the objective - and return those property names from [code]_get_replicated_properties[/code] to have the framework keep them in step.
	</description>
